## What each part name means

Every part name is ruled once, for the whole dataset. A name ruled to a class means that
class wherever it occurs. A name ruled *ambiguous* has no class that fits it, and the
ontology only grows from the training split; its parts are judged as objects and as ends
of relations, but not on their class. An *ignored* name is left out of the evaluation with
its parts. Counts are parts in the kept scenes.

